  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` as `docs/SPEC.md` describes it. `npm test` passes: 7 tests, 0 failed.\n\n- **Behaviour:** it covers every form in the spec, including the prerelease rule. It returns `false` for an invalid version or range, and never throws. I used `BigInt` for the numeric parts so very large version numbers compare exactly.\n- **Choices where the spec is silent:**\n  - Leading zeros in prerelease identifiers are allowed.\n  - `>*` and `<*` match nothing.\n  - An empty piece of a `||` range, such as `\"1.0.0 ||\"`, means \"any version\".\n  - A range is invalid as a whole if any piece of it is invalid.\n- **Tests:** the new `test/satisfies.test.js` covers matching and non-matching cases for each spec table, prerelease ordering, invalid versions and ranges, and large numbers. Two of my first expectations were wrong, not the code, and I corrected them.",
